# Dashboard Home and tabs

## Composition (My dashboards · director Today)

1. Toolbar: filter **icon** opens a **modal** (period, warehouse, currency). No full-width filter bar (and no second Filters toolbar row on feature tabs).
2. KPI strip: one **Sales hero** + five side metrics (Profit, Cash to collect, Trucks on the road, Stock at risk, Margin). No colored left status borders; RAG via value/chip tone only.
3. Row: **Decisions** (narrow) | **Sales and profit** | **Stock cover**.
4. **Money owed** full width: ageing chart beside top balances (not one stretched bar alone).
5. Off default Today: top products and sales distribution. Those sit on Sales.

## Feature tabs

- One report per tab. Order is `REPORT` in `room.ts`. Do not add an Advanced / normal switch.
- Prefer **paired charts** (ageing | top list, bridge | donut, month | share) over one full-width stretched series.
- A card is only as tall as its content. Do not stretch a short card up to a longer neighbour. A long list scrolls inside the card. The chart face is the chart; the table is the icon toggle, not a second block under the chart.
- Exception: on the overview, the truck map sits under the stats in the same row as the charts. That row stretches, and the map grows to the bottom of the charts. Do not leave an empty band under the map.
- Business is the operations glance: sales, profit and margin, prices below target, and landed cost per product. The profit bridge, monthly trend and brand ranking stay on Management. Trip cost per truck stays on Fees.
- A section that repeats a panel already on the tab stays in `hiddenReport`. Border heatmap, fast and slow, and landed cost are part of the report, not a second mode.

Mockup reference: Cursor canvas `home-today-mockup.canvas.tsx`. Product narrative: `docs/21-dashboard-redesign.md`.

## Language

- **Title** = short noun phrase (≤ ~4 words). Use catalogue `r.title` on feature panels.
- **No** What / Which / How / Where / Who question titles.
- **Caption** = period / unit only, inside the info icon. Not a line under the title.
- **Decision** = one imperative sentence, inside the exclamation icon. Not a line under the title.
- Chart header is one flex row: title, info icon, recommendation icon, then chart | table and export.
- **Drill** = "Open …", not "View details".
- **No em dashes (—)** in product copy. Prefer commas, periods, or hyphens. Empty cells: `-`.

## Color

- UI chrome: logo navy + orange accent (CTA only). Warning = yellow-amber, never logo orange as chart status.
- Dark mode, on an orange surface: titles are white (`--text-on-primary`), supporting text is blue (`--text-on-primary-muted`), and icons, counts and status marks are yellow (`--on-primary-accent`). Do not put dark navy text on orange. Same roles on a navy primary surface in light mode.
- Decisions is navy in light mode and `--attention` blue in dark mode, so it reads as the thing to clear first. Do not paint it orange. The icon, status word and count take their colour from urgency: critical red, high amber, watch a lighter yellow, clear green.
- Chart series (control-room): navy sales, teal, amber, green profit, cost salmon. Home sales/profit lines use those series inks.

## Type

- Display (Montserrat): page H1, section card titles.
- Body (Inter): captions, tables, decision rows, KPI labels.
- Tabular nums on money and counts.

## Chart ↔ table

- Icon pair on each chart card (chart | table). Graph default. Icons only with aria-label.
- Prefer two compact charts side by side when a single series would stretch across a wide card.
